2026-10-19T00:32:12.0528725Z [36;1mfi[0m
2026-10-19T00:32:12.0529492Z [36;1m# THE REUSABLE WORKFLOW SHIPS INSTANTLY VIA @main; THE SCRIPT IT RUNS DOES NOT.[0m
2026-10-19T00:32:12.0530240Z [36;1m# This invokes the CONSUMER's `tools/coverage_trend.py`, a sync-managed file COPY that[0m
2026-10-19T00:32:12.0530989Z [36;1m# only arrives on the next maint-68 run (daily, 05:00 UTC). So for one sync window this[0m
2026-10-19T00:32:12.0531718Z [36;1m# workflow is newer than the script it calls, and passing a flag the older script does[0m
2026-10-19T00:32:12.0532465Z [36;1m# not know makes argparse exit 2 and fails the step -- in every consumer at once.[0m
2026-10-19T00:32:12.0533230Z [36;1m# Probe instead of assume; the flag is optional by design (the script defaults to cwd,[0m
2026-10-19T00:32:12.0533969Z [36;1m# which is already correct for every `working-directory: "."` consumer). Remove this[0m
